# Every file in this repository is byte-exact by design.
#
# 2026-08-27: the first push let git normalise line endings, and a fresh clone
# reported `verify: FAIL | drift 40` — forty files whose bytes no longer matched
# the hashes recorded for them. Nothing was wrong with the artifacts; git had
# rewritten them on checkout. A reader's first command would have shown our own
# integrity check declaring our own release corrupt.
#
# `-text` disables end-of-line conversion for everything. In a repository whose
# entire claim is that recorded hashes still hold, a convenience that silently
# edits files on checkout is not a convenience.
* -text
